# Tourism Data ETL Pipeline Project Documentation

## Project Overview

The Tourism credit card Data ETL Pipeline project was developed to automate the extraction, transformation, validation, and storage of tourism-related credit card data. The pipeline processes raw tourism credit card datasets, cleans and standardizes the data, validates data quality, detects anomalies, and generates a cleaned dataset ready for analytics and reporting.

The project was implemented using Apache Airflow for workflow orchestration, Docker for containerization, and Python (Pandas) for data processing.

---

# Project Objectives

The main objectives of the project were:

* Automate tourism credit card data processing.
* Improve data quality through cleaning and validation.
* Detect and handle missing or inconsistent records.
* Standardize column names and data types.
* Generate a clean dataset for downstream analytics.
* Schedule and monitor data processing workflows using Airflow.
* Containerize the environment for portability and reproducibility.

